WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.240
When you think about what Beijing is known for.&nbsp;
snow doesn't come to mind. It only snows about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.880
four days a year. Yet that didn't stop the&nbsp;
International Olympic Committee from awarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:17.280
it the Winter Games in 2022. There weren't a lot&nbsp;
of options. The only other contender was Almaty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.760
Kazakhstan. Even though the Olympics&nbsp;
are the pride and joy of a country,&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.920
most don't want to host the Games anymore. A&nbsp;
record 11 cities bid for the 2004 Olympics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.520
That dwindled down to five for 2020 and it's&nbsp;
kept falling. After three cities dropped out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:39.520
the 2024 race, that left Paris and Los Angeles,&nbsp;
so the IOC gave them to the French capital and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:45.760
decided LA would do the honors in 2028. So why&nbsp;
does no one want to host the Olympics anymore?

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.520
The Olympic Games are really expensive to host.&nbsp;
Every single one in the past few decades has gone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.840
over their estimated cost and the postponed 2020&nbsp;
Tokyo Olympics are expected to be no different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.920
And you, the taxpayer, are responsible&nbsp;
for paying a good portion of the bill.&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:10.480
Beijing's Bird's Nest stadium for the 2008&nbsp;
Olympics cost $480 million. Located not too far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.080
away is the Aquatics Center - $140 million. Then&nbsp;
there's the Olympic Village where the athletes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:22.320
live. Rio de Janeiro built these condos for $700&nbsp;
million which was actually not a lot compared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:28.640
the $3 billion subway line that didn't even extend&nbsp;
all the way to the Olympic venue. And ever since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:35.280
2001, security costs have gone up with London&nbsp;
dishing out $870 million for its 2012 Games.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.360
So many other expenses that might not be obvious&nbsp;
can add up, like building hotels in some cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:47.840
because the IOC requires 40,000 rooms be available&nbsp;
for the Summer Games, or reserving special lanes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.360
for athletes and officials and having a media&nbsp;
center for journalists which is not cheap.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.880
Networks pay a lot for the rights to broadcast the&nbsp;
Games and spending has soared over the years. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:04.640
host city gets some of the revenue but less than&nbsp;
they used to. The IOC pockets about half of it. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.280
the end, cities have been spending more than they&nbsp;
earn and they justify the costs in the hopes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:15.200
Games will leave behind a legacy. But in the case&nbsp;
of Brazil, it's not the legacy they wanted. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:21.120
Rio de Janeiro became the first South American&nbsp;
city to host the Olympics in 2016, it was a moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.160
of national pride. Most of the sporting events&nbsp;
took place in a remote region in the western&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.000
zone of Rio at the newly built Olympic Park for&nbsp;
half a billion U.S. But when the Games ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.800
everything fell apart. In January 2020, a judge&nbsp;
ordered it shut down over safety concerns. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.000
iconic Maracanã Stadium, which held the opening&nbsp;
and closing ceremonies was abandoned after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.120
Games. Vandals ripped out thousands of seats. The&nbsp;
state was so saddled down by the $13 billion cost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.400
of the Games, it couldn't pay its teachers on time&nbsp;
let alone take care of its Olympic venues. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.520
athletes' village was supposed to sell as luxury&nbsp;
condos but most of the units still sit empty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.360
People are speaking out about the consequences of&nbsp;
hosting the Games. A group in Boston actually put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:14.880
a stop to their city's 2024 bid. So is it possible&nbsp;
there could be no Olympics one day? The IOC knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:20.560
there's a problem. In its 2020 agenda, it listed&nbsp;
recommendations as it's done in previous years to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.760
shape the future of the Olympic movement. One&nbsp;
of the key points is including sustainability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.120
in all aspects of the Games which also means&nbsp;
making sure the Games don't break the bank.&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.480
That will be put to the test in 2024. Organizers&nbsp;
of the Paris GameS say they're pretty much using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.960
what they have instead of building more because&nbsp;
95% of the infrastructure it needs already exists.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.240
Beach volleyball will be played&nbsp;
by the Champs de Mars green space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.120
Archery will take place outside Les Invalides,
a complex of museums and monuments.&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.000
Fencing in taekwondo will be held inside&nbsp;
the historic exhibition hall Grand Palais.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.120
Making the most of what you have worked out for&nbsp;
Los Angeles when it hardly constructed any venues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:07.680
for the 1984 Olympics and made a profit of $250&nbsp;
million. LA didn't feel the pressure to build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:14.800
after seeing how the 1976 Games nearly broke&nbsp;
Montreal. The Olympic Stadium alone cost over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.960
$1 billion, It took Canadians 30 years to pay off&nbsp;
the debt and the province of Quebec still spends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:26.720
millions maintaining the stadium even though no&nbsp;
major sports team uses it. Avoiding maintenance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.160
fees is the reason Pyeongchang decided to&nbsp;
tear down the $100 million stadium it built&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.120
specifically for the opening and closing&nbsp;
ceremonies of its 2018 Winter Games.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.240
And to really save on costs, there's the idea&nbsp;
floating around of having a permanent host city -&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.320
although some argue this would tarnish&nbsp;
the global nature of the Olympics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:52.560
But it's clear more and more cities are struggling&nbsp;
to afford the Games. For the 2026 Winter Games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.680
once again only two contenders put up their&nbsp;
hand. The Italian duo of Milan and the ski&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.800
resort Cortina d'Ampezzo beat out the Swedish&nbsp;
duo. But this doesn't mean the Olympics will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:08.560
be gone for good. The Olympic Games were never&nbsp;
just about sports. It's a way for countries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.520
show off their progress on the world stage which&nbsp;
is why it's no coincidence Russia and China have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:20.400
been the biggest spenders. Beijing's $40 billion
Games were only eclipsed by the $51 billion Russia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:27.280
spent on Sochi in 2014 - the most expensive ever.&nbsp;
So long as these countries continue to spend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:33.200
the show will go on. But if the IOC wants to see&nbsp;
more diversity among the host city candidates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:39.440
there has to be a new kind of Olympics. One that&nbsp;
brings home the medals but leaves the debt behind.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.520
Hey guys, thanks so much&nbsp;
for watching. I'm Cindy Pom.

